gredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Chinese sausages are the different types of sausages with ties to China, the Sinosphere or the Chinese diaspora."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chinese-sausage"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_sausage"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Bánh bao","dish/banh-bao"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Mushroom","ingredient/mushroom"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/60/Chinese_dried_sausages_in_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-Chinese_dried_sausages_in_Hong_Kong.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Peachyeung316","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinese_dried_sausages_in_Hong_Kong.jpg"}},"dish/english-muffin":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/english-muffin","n":"English muffin","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["An English muffin is a small, round, flat yeast-leavened (sometimes sourdough) bread which is commonly about 4 in (10 cm) in diameter and 1.5 in (4 cm) tall. It is generally split horizontally and served toasted. They are unsweetened and frequently eaten with sweet or savoury toppings, such as butter, fruit jam, honey, eggs, sausage, bacon, or cheese. English muffins are an essential ingredient in eggs Benedict and a variety of breakfast sandwiches derived from it, such as the McMuffin."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-english-muffin"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_muffin"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Milk","ingre