ng_English_muffins_03.jpg","w":500,"h":374,"by":"Jennifer from Columbia, South Carolina, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_jspatchwork_146937146--Making_English_muffins_03.jpg"}},"ingredient/snakehead-fish":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/snakehead-fish","n":"Snakehead (fish)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The snakeheads are members of the freshwater perciform fish family Channidae, native to parts of Africa and Asia. These elongated, predatory fish are distinguished by their long dorsal fins, large mouths, and shiny teeth. They breathe air with gills, which allows them to migrate short distances over land. They have suprabranchial organs, which are primitive forms of labyrinth organs, that develop when they grow older. The two extant genera are Channa in Asia and Parachanna in Africa, consisting of more than 50 species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-snakehead-fish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakehead_(fish)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Khô cá lóc","dish/kho-ca-loc"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Channidae","ingredient/channidae"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f8/Snakehead_-_Channa_argus_2.jpg/500px-Snakehead_-_Channa_argus_2.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Brian Gratwicke","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snakehead_-_Channa_argus_2.jpg"}},"dish/liangfen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/liangfen","n":"Liangfen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Liangfen, also spelled liang fen, is a Chinese legume dish consisting of starch jelly that is usually served cold, with a savory sauce, often in the summer. It is most popular in northern China, including Beijing, Gansu, and Shaanxi, but may also be found in Sichuan and Qinghai. In Tibet and Nepal it is called laping and is a common street vendor food. In Kyrgyzstan it is an ingredient in a noodle dish called ashlan fu."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-liangfen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liangfen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Huangqiao sesame cake","dish/huangqiao-sesame-cake"],["Imitation shark fin soup","dish/imitation-shark-fin-soup"],["Jiaozi","dish/jiaozi"],["Jiuqu","dish/jiuqu"],["Kung Pao chicken","dish/kung-pao-chicken"],["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"],["Lo mai chi","dish/lo-mai-chi"],["Mao xue wang","dish/mao-xue-wang"],["Mapo tofu","dish/mapo-tofu"],["Mianwo","dish/mianwo"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Orange cuttlefish","dish/orange-cuttlefish"],["Osmanthus cake","dish/osmanthus-cake"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/97/Liangpi-sichuan.jpg/500px-Liangpi-sichuan.jpg","w":500,"h":259,"by":"Prince Roy","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liangpi-sichuan.jpg"}},"dish/mola-salsa":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mola-salsa","n":"Mola salsa","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Ancient Roman cuisine","dot":"#a99fb5","intro":[["In ancient Roman religion, mola salsa (\"salted flour\") was a mixture of coarse-ground, toasted emmer flour and salt prepared by the Vestal Virgins and used in every official sacrifice. It was sprinkled on the forehead and between the horns of animal victims before they were sacrificed, as well as on the altar and in the sacred fire. It was a common offering to the household hearth."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mola-salsa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mola_salsa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Ancient Roman cuisine","cuisine/ancient-roman-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Farro","ingredient/farro"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pass the Garum","ref":"site/pass-the-garum-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pass-the-garum.blogspot.com","note":"Blog by an ancient history graduate recreating Roman recipes as closely as possible to the sources; may no longer be updated.","url":"https://pass-the-garum.blogspot.com/p/about-me.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]}]},"dish/pindjur":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pindjur","n":"Pindjur","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pindjur or pinjur or pinđur is a red-pepper spread or relish often used in summer and autumn. Pindjur is commonly prepared in  Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, Bulgaria, Serbia, Kosovo and North Macedonia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pindjur"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pindjur"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine"],["Macedonian cuisine","cuisine/macedonian-cuisine"],["Serbian cuisine","cuisine/serbian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Balkan Lunchbox: Kosovo recipes","ref":"site/balkanlunchbox-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"balkanlunchbox.com","note":"Balkan home cooking blog with a section of Serbian dishes.","url":"https://balkanlunchbox.com/category/country/serbian-recipes/page/3","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Bulgarian cuisine","links":[["Banitsa","dish/banitsa"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Garash cake","dish/garash-cake"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Lyutenitsa","dish/lyutenitsa"],["Patatnik","dish/patatnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tarator","dish/tarator"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5e/Pindjur2.JPG/500px-Pindjur2.JPG","w":500,"h":420,"by":"Off-shell","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindjur2.JPG"}},"ingredient/pomace":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pomace","n":"Pomace","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Pomace, pumace (, PUM-əs) or marc (; from French marc [maʁ]) is the solid remains of grapes, olives, or other fruit after pressing for juice or oil. It contains the skins, pulp, seeds, and stems of the fruit."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pomace"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomace"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Rakı","dish/rak"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Barrel","ingredient/barrel"],["Date","ingredient/date"],["Fig","ingredient/fig"],["Grape","ingredient/grape"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/1/15/Mthomebrew_pomace.JPG","w":500,"h":846,"by":"Agne27 at the English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mthomebrew_pomace.JPG"}},"dish/rassolnik":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rassolnik","n":"Rassolnik","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Russian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Rassolnik is a traditional Russian soup made from pickled cucumbers, pearl barley, and pork or beef kidneys. A vegetarian variant of rassolnik also exists, usually made during Lent. The dish is known to have existed as far back as the 15th century, when it was called kalya. Rassolnik became part of the common Soviet cuisine and today it is also popular in Ukraine (as rozsoljnyk) and Belarus (as rasoljnik). A similar dish is common in Poland, where it is known as zupa ogórkowa (literally 'cucumber soup')."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rassolnik"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rassolnik"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Kidney","ingredient/kidney"],["Kidneys as food","ingredient/kidneys-as-food"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","ref":"site/olgasflavorfactory-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Khrenovina sauce","dish/khrenovina-sauce"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce",